#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054381 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054834 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4007f63e-0a99-57ca-a1f6-190b21f02ecc" :knowledge-point/title "Linear Equations Requiring Multiplication by a Positive Integer"}] :question/id #uuid "c64cd16e-2f9d-5564-8d04-eddcad2c5d01" :question/math-academy-id "e-12859" :question/problem "Find the value of $q$ that satisfies the equation $\\dfrac{q}{4}=-9.$" :question/worked-solution "In the equation, $q$ is being divided by $4.$ To isolate $q$, we can perform the opposite operation, which is *multiplying* by $4$. So, we multiply both sides of the equation by $4.$\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel}\n\t\\eqalign{\n    \t\t\\dfrac{q}{4} &=-9\\[5pt]\n\t\t4\\cdot \\dfrac{q}{4} &=4\\cdot \\left(-9\\right) \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac{4q}{4} &= -36\n\t}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $4$ from both the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel}\n\t\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac{4q}{4} &= -36 \\[5pt]\n                \\dfrac{\\cancel{4}q}{\\cancel{4}} &= -36 \\\n\t\tq &=-36\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054382 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "712bc4c6-aeaf-5081-9e64-791027b38963" :knowledge-point/title "Linear Equations Requiring Multiplication by a Negative Integer"}] :question/id #uuid "5fe35108-2fa8-563e-862e-ad27d4ed5334" :question/math-academy-id "e-12860" :question/problem "Find the value of $k$ that satisfies the equation $-\\dfrac{k}{2}=\\dfrac{1}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's remove the negative sign from the variable. To do this, we multiply both sides of the equation by $-1.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{k}{2} & =\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-\\frac{k}{2}) & =(-1)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\ \\frac{k}{2} & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the equation above, $k$ is being divided by $2.$ To isolate $k$, we can perform the opposite operation, which is *multiplying* by $2$. So, we multiply both sides of the equation by $2$ and simplify.\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel}\n\t\\eqalign{\n    \t\t\\dfrac{k}{2} &=-\\dfrac{1}{3} \\[5pt]\n\t\t2 \\cdot \\dfrac{k}{2} &=2 \\cdot \\left( -\\dfrac{1}{3} \\right) \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac{2k}{2} &= -\\dfrac{2}{3} \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac{\\cancel{2}k}{\\cancel{2}} &= -\\dfrac{2}{3} \\[5pt]\n\t\tk &= -\\dfrac{2}{3}\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054383 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e153c18d-6f3e-5fef-a006-c5597cd88bc9" :knowledge-point/title "Linear Equations Requiring Division"}] :question/id #uuid "68865bc2-e4e2-53d9-9988-4fa962e04746" :question/math-academy-id "e-12861" :question/problem "Solve the equation $24=-3z.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the equation in a way that's a little more familiar to us. We can do this by swapping the left and right-hand sides of the equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}24 & =-3z \\\\ -3z & =24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the variable $z$ is being *multiplied* by $-3.$ To isolate $z$, we can perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $-3$. So, we divide both sides of the equation by $-3$ and simplify.\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel}\n\t\\eqalign{\n    \t\t-3z &=24 \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac {-3z} {-3} &= \\dfrac {24} {-3} \\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac {\\cancel{-3}z} {\\cancel{-3}} &= -8 \\[5pt]\n\t\tz &=-8\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054388 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054835 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b765f7b2-639a-5519-9170-02a4fcb0f8fe" :knowledge-point/title "Cases Where the Variable Is on the Right-Hand Side"}] :question/id #uuid "cbce1708-81ba-5d37-ae21-fc8d94ebbc2f" :question/math-academy-id "e-12894" :question/problem "If $\\dfrac{1}{7}=\\dfrac{x}{2},$ then $x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x}{2}=\\dfrac{1}{7}\n$$\n\nIn this equation, $x$ is being divided by $2.$ To isolate $x$, we can perform the opposite operation, which is *multiplying* by $2.$ So, we multiply both sides of the equation by $2$ and simplify.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & =\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ 2\\cdot \\frac{x}{2} & =2\\cdot (\\frac{1}{7}) \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & =\\frac{2}{7} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{2}x}{\\cancel{2}} & =\\frac{2}{7} \\\\ x & =\\frac{2}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479893 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054834 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4007f63e-0a99-57ca-a1f6-190b21f02ecc" :knowledge-point/title "Linear Equations Requiring Multiplication by a Positive Integer"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "084da45d-5363-5cef-bc65-730f06261b96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c=35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479372} {:answer/id #uuid "974a8c26-2e0e-5e3c-b504-5c1eb40a74c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c=105" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479588} {:answer/id #uuid "b3d61de8-e89c-5958-aeba-2ee8b2dc43db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c=-35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479627} {:answer/id #uuid "b8bfe55b-3f3f-5437-9c1c-534c75c79276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c=-105" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479636} {:answer/id #uuid "e2f64205-9c2f-5594-9863-ad6b055ee69f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c=-75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479692}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8bfe55b-3f3f-5437-9c1c-534c75c79276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c=-105" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479636} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccb0d861-b055-54be-9807-8167d461f080" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479804}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d37f3cd3-5a50-54b2-83fb-c1289723c204" :question/math-academy-id "q-101703" :question/problem "If $\\frac{c}{7}=-15,$ then $c=$" :question/worked-solution "In the equation, $c$ is being divided by $7.$ To isolate $c$, we can perform the opposite operation, which is *multiplying* by $7.$ So, we multiply both sides of the equation by $7.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{c}{7} & =-15 \\\\ 7\\cdot \\frac{c}{7} & =7\\cdot (-15) \\\\ \\frac{7c}{7} & =-105\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $7$ from both the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7c}{7} & =-105 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{7}c}{\\cancel{7}} & =-105 \\\\ c & =-105\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479891 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e153c18d-6f3e-5fef-a006-c5597cd88bc9" :knowledge-point/title "Linear Equations Requiring Division"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0297944e-94e0-59aa-b8df-3fc18b5681ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479363} {:answer/id #uuid "1ddcb64c-c357-54cf-89aa-030f369b98da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479408} {:answer/id #uuid "311a4202-38ac-552b-88a0-fc11ccd2885b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479436} {:answer/id #uuid "8c4c33f7-864c-57ab-a135-6d02a1174278" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479567} {:answer/id #uuid "936c1241-d294-5cd8-ac4e-a80dd3d0c1ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479581}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "936c1241-d294-5cd8-ac4e-a80dd3d0c1ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479581} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d13bba6-2073-5396-8480-40096b0cd49a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479765}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d1c0c05b-9184-5c94-9e0b-29a6b0d0aa2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-101709" :question/problem "If $-5t=-60$, then $t=$" :question/worked-solution "The variable $t$ is being *multiplied* by $-5.$ To isolate $t$, we can perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $-5.$ So, we divide both sides of the equation by $-5.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5t & =-60 \\\\ \\frac{-5t}{-5} & =\\frac{-60}{-5} \\\\ \\frac{-5t}{-5} & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $-5$ from both the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-5t}{-5} & =12 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-5}t}{\\cancel{-5}} & =12 \\\\ t & =12\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479844 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e153c18d-6f3e-5fef-a006-c5597cd88bc9" :knowledge-point/title "Linear Equations Requiring Division"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "496138ed-80d7-5019-be5a-71780dc2805f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479468} {:answer/id #uuid "5d5c1bdb-c6b7-54e7-8566-5bc991faef09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479491} {:answer/id #uuid "6005c5b4-9cc1-503a-b9b4-c160b3cd0c82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479499} {:answer/id #uuid "b866fa1c-8177-59ba-9e67-1bfd52204486" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479634} {:answer/id #uuid "f0044bd4-9712-58b9-98a7-e554f9df6582" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479717}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "496138ed-80d7-5019-be5a-71780dc2805f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479468} :answer-field/id #uuid "f974a2a4-9c4f-5a1b-821e-f099326de82a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479822}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3418ccb3-fdc3-5d51-a5fe-8860e2e0eae1" :question/math-academy-id "q-104729" :question/problem "If $-8x=-56$, then $x=$" :question/worked-solution "The variable $x$ is being *multiplied* by $-8.$ To isolate $x$, we can perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $-8.$ So, we divide both sides of the equation by $-8.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8x & =-56 \\\\ \\frac{-8x}{-8} & =\\frac{-56}{-8} \\\\ \\frac{-8x}{-8} & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $-8$ from both the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-8x}{-8} & =7 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-8}x}{\\cancel{-8}} & =7 \\\\ x & =7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479865 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054835 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b765f7b2-639a-5519-9170-02a4fcb0f8fe" :knowledge-point/title "Cases Where the Variable Is on the Right-Hand Side"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01b5e5a5-95aa-50c9-9d76-ccae8d506b80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479361} {:answer/id #uuid "4799234a-295a-5198-942b-53a5d2def29a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479464} {:answer/id #uuid "bc91284d-02f4-5fa0-a83d-e7d598cec96a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479643} {:answer/id #uuid "d6c53334-5e62-56b4-b272-6771b213342e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479683} {:answer/id #uuid "f7b72569-c5f7-531a-a000-407c5565a4ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4799234a-295a-5198-942b-53a5d2def29a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479464} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb6e90f1-e4fb-5bd7-934a-abea3bb1a854" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479816}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7ce50429-066c-52cc-b521-7f9c1d989259" :question/math-academy-id "q-185208" :question/problem "If $4=\\frac{x}{6},$ then $x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{6}=4\n$$\n\nIn this equation, $x$ is being divided by $6.$ To isolate $x$, we can perform the opposite operation, which is *multiplying* by $6.$ So, we multiply both sides of the equation by $6$ and simplify.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{6} & =4 \\\\ 6\\cdot \\frac{x}{6} & =6\\cdot 4 \\\\ \\frac{6x}{6} & =24 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{6}x}{\\cancel{6}} & =24 \\\\ x & =24\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479828 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054835 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b765f7b2-639a-5519-9170-02a4fcb0f8fe" :knowledge-point/title "Cases Where the Variable Is on the Right-Hand Side"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16d6e6db-a830-5baa-9915-b9601554ab12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479395} {:answer/id #uuid "202536e5-08f9-5281-b8f2-6dfd148bd8a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479412} {:answer/id #uuid "2dc9aebe-c25e-5476-b79f-e7304f0323b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479427} {:answer/id #uuid "2ea01f77-9bfa-55a9-acf1-b7a14f6df61a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479429} {:answer/id #uuid "9dc5900f-7d6d-5fab-bd02-49a64c159f82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479599}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16d6e6db-a830-5baa-9915-b9601554ab12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479395} :answer-field/id #uuid "8dfedb67-9d0d-5a04-828e-a8b8e90aee86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479789}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "063f6e3f-2db2-5183-9271-70afe486d5c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-185213" :question/problem "If $-5=\\frac{t}{4},$ then $t=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\frac{t}{4}=-5\n$$\n\nIn this equation, $t$ is being divided by $4.$ To isolate $t$, we can perform the opposite operation, which is *multiplying* by $4.$ So, we multiply both sides of the equation by $4$ and simplify.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{t}{4} & =-5 \\\\ 4\\cdot \\frac{t}{4} & =4\\cdot (-5) \\\\ \\frac{4t}{4} & =-20 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{4}t}{\\cancel{4}} & =-20 \\\\ t & =-20\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479855 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054834 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4007f63e-0a99-57ca-a1f6-190b21f02ecc" :knowledge-point/title "Linear Equations Requiring Multiplication by a Positive Integer"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "325d0450-9b16-5aac-a3a7-377751f4e94b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479438} {:answer/id #uuid "89661690-95ae-56d1-8974-7e150a0d7ba9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479562} {:answer/id #uuid "8f77c9df-4ac8-595b-8f02-822b5fbff059" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479576} {:answer/id #uuid "9a1f099e-c9e5-5616-be0b-79e83962f791" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479594} {:answer/id #uuid "cc244fbe-3e9f-5073-a784-ed1931a0a3de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f77c9df-4ac8-595b-8f02-822b5fbff059" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479576} :answer-field/id #uuid "f59d6512-b95a-5889-be9a-ac13bd918ef5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "559e6eeb-8cf0-577b-a9ee-88ad70f4ec15" :question/math-academy-id "q-2529" :question/problem "If $\\frac{y}{3}=-7,$ then $y=$" :question/worked-solution "In the equation, $y$ is being *divided* by $3.$ To isolate $y$, we can perform the opposite operation, which is *multiplying* by $3.$ So, we multiply both sides of the equation by $3.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{3} & =-7 \\\\ 3\\cdot \\frac{y}{3} & =3\\cdot (-7) \\\\ \\frac{3y}{3} & =-21\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $3$ from both the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3y}{3} & =-21 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{3}y}{\\cancel{3}} & =-21 \\\\ y & =-21\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479831 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "712bc4c6-aeaf-5081-9e64-791027b38963" :knowledge-point/title "Linear Equations Requiring Multiplication by a Negative Integer"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13ab2acd-ac6c-5c2a-995c-c1dee89cbd43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479388} {:answer/id #uuid "1909a1c9-6691-531d-93d0-870e5d5ef65a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479399} {:answer/id #uuid "2fbc6af7-9db2-57c1-834c-568900349313" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479433} {:answer/id #uuid "ac3c64de-c016-5a5b-8e71-f84fd4be4d25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479614} {:answer/id #uuid "df4336c2-5480-5d1a-a84d-7019f790df07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479688}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fbc6af7-9db2-57c1-834c-568900349313" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479433} :answer-field/id #uuid "bde93567-ec99-5785-851e-83145a289d18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479800}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0b5cb4d7-77e4-5ac4-8439-cb36ef6f1c98" :question/math-academy-id "q-6233" :question/problem "If $-\\frac{x}{7}=-3,$ then $x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's remove the negative sign from the variable. To do this, we multiply both sides of the equation by $-1.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{x}{7} & =-3 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-\\frac{x}{7}) & =(-1)\\cdot (-3) \\\\ \\frac{x}{7} & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the equation above, $x$ is being *divided* by $7.$ To isolate $x$, we can perform the opposite operation, which is *multiplying* by $7.$ So, we multiply both sides of the equation by $7$ and simplify.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{7} & =3 \\\\ 7\\cdot \\frac{x}{7} & =7\\cdot 3 \\\\ \\frac{7x}{7} & =21 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{7}x}{\\cancel{7}} & =21 \\\\ x & =21\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479882 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "712bc4c6-aeaf-5081-9e64-791027b38963" :knowledge-point/title "Linear Equations Requiring Multiplication by a Negative Integer"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b5bfd06-95e1-5941-b827-ceeac852f83e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479375} {:answer/id #uuid "3256080f-70d0-5fb8-a894-8e796e21fcea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479437} {:answer/id #uuid "4c88a484-7f77-57a9-b38b-ae25dd456160" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479473} {:answer/id #uuid "55dcc1fb-ebd9-55f7-95ad-86544ff060eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479480} {:answer/id #uuid "60abafac-8bc5-5541-a465-e3ddc61858bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60abafac-8bc5-5541-a465-e3ddc61858bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479501} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8961cfc-c61f-5d7e-9ac8-9ae2e5f043be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479809}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b4c0e9de-946c-5a43-9beb-5626829b00ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-75388" :question/problem "If $-\\frac{c}{12}=4,$ then $c=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's remove the negative sign from the variable. To do this, we multiply both sides of the equation by $-1.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{c}{12} & =4 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-\\frac{c}{12}) & =(-1)\\cdot 4 \\\\ \\frac{c}{12} & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the equation above, $c$ is being divided by $12.$ To isolate $c$, we can perform the opposite operation, which is *multiplying* by $12.$ So, we multiply both sides of the equation by $12$ and simplify.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{c}{12} & =-4 \\\\ 12\\cdot \\frac{c}{12} & =12\\cdot (-4) \\\\ \\frac{12c}{12} & =-48 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{12}c}{\\cancel{12}} & =-48 \\\\ c & =-48\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
